WEBVTT

00:06.387 --> 00:09.890
<i>Rise and shine.
Welcome to Morioh Radio,</i>

00:09.974 --> 00:11.600
<i>Kai Harada, here,</i>

00:11.684 --> 00:14.353
<i>keeping you company
on this fine morning.</i>

00:14.771 --> 00:17.440
<i>And I've got just
the melody to start you off right…</i>

00:35.583 --> 00:38.043
Well, shall we dig in?

00:38.127 --> 00:41.213
Of course. How could I forget…

01:22.046 --> 01:22.796
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:22.797 --> 01:24.924
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

01:24.966 --> 01:27.301
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

01:27.343 --> 01:30.596
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

01:31.347 --> 01:33.474
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

01:33.516 --> 01:35.851
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

01:35.935 --> 01:39.188
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

01:39.397 --> 01:42.900
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

01:43.693 --> 01:47.113
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

01:47.155 --> 01:49.782
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

01:49.824 --> 01:51.992
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

01:52.035 --> 01:54.037
<i>I will chase you</i>

01:54.120 --> 01:55.746
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

01:55.830 --> 01:58.374
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

01:58.458 --> 02:00.501
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

02:00.543 --> 02:03.254
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

02:03.463 --> 02:07.963
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

02:09.177 --> 02:13.677
<i>So I chase you</i>

02:16.976 --> 02:21.313
EPISODE 21
YOSHIKAGE KIRA JUST
WANTS TO LIVE QUIETLY, PART 1

02:17.810 --> 02:20.062
Mr. Kira… Um, Mr. Kira?

02:25.318 --> 02:29.818
Mr. Kira, if you have nothing else to do,
would you like to have lunch with us?

02:31.491 --> 02:33.826
My apologies, but I must decline.

02:34.369 --> 02:37.789
These documents need delivering.

02:38.247 --> 02:39.665
Cheerio.

02:41.918 --> 02:43.377
Don't waste your time!

02:44.295 --> 02:46.338
He'll just end up
being the downer of the group.

02:46.714 --> 02:48.924
Every time we've had him come along,

02:48.966 --> 02:51.051
you can't tell if he's
happy or completely miserable…

02:51.636 --> 02:55.056
Yoshikage Kira, age 33, single.

02:55.306 --> 02:57.433
He really is the consummate worker,

02:57.558 --> 02:59.893
but, man, the guy is
dull as dishwater.

03:00.520 --> 03:05.020
He's not necessarily a bad guy,
it's just he has no personality.

03:11.406 --> 03:15.117
Well, someone's a little
bent out of shape…

03:14.325 --> 03:18.825
SAVORY BREAD / GARLIC BREAD /
APPLE PIE / SLICED BREAD / MILK BREAD / RUSKS /
CROISSANTS / DONUTS /
PIZZA BREAD / CORNBREAD

03:15.368 --> 03:19.538
Those new girls at work
invited me to lunch, that's all.

03:19.956 --> 03:23.125
I promised you
lunch was our time together.

03:23.084 --> 03:27.584
CHOCOLATE MUFFINS

03:23.292 --> 03:26.211
I'd never leave you
to go with them.

03:26.921 --> 03:29.172
You heard me turn them down,
didn't you?

03:28.589 --> 03:29.631
CHOCOLATE MUFFINS
SLICED BREAD / CROISSANTS

03:30.133 --> 03:33.803
Have I ever left you
by your lonesome?

03:36.222 --> 03:38.682
Now, stop this silly fretting,

03:38.808 --> 03:41.310
and let's pick out
some sandwiches.

03:39.767 --> 03:44.267
KATSU SANDWICH

03:41.477 --> 03:43.562
Now, which one do you want?

03:43.730 --> 03:45.815
It has such a delicate texture,
doesn't it?

03:45.982 --> 03:47.817
This bakery makes its sandwiches

03:47.859 --> 03:52.359
with bread it bakes fresh at 11 AM;
they're all the rage.

03:52.780 --> 03:55.449
You'd be lucky to
find one on the shelf after 1 PM.

03:55.950 --> 03:58.702
You can feel they're fresh
from the oven through the wrapper.

03:59.036 --> 04:02.497
The katsu they use is
always freshly fried and perfectly crispy.

04:05.042 --> 04:06.334
Look at that…

04:06.461 --> 04:10.298
You tore the wrapper
and made a mess.

04:11.549 --> 04:13.008
Such a naughty girl.

04:28.483 --> 04:32.111
But now this sandwich is ruined,

04:32.153 --> 04:34.446
we'll just buy
the one underneath.

04:35.156 --> 04:36.949
Thank you for dropping by.

04:51.172 --> 04:54.925
Beautiful, isn't it?
Quaint, little Morioh…

04:55.343 --> 04:58.721
It might just be the most
marvelous town on earth…

04:59.180 --> 05:02.224
It's like we're on a picnic.

05:14.987 --> 05:17.155
<i>A bit aromatic…</i>

05:17.198 --> 05:20.367
<i>I think it maybe time
we part ways…</i>

05:20.451 --> 05:22.161
<i>The end is close at hand.</i>

05:22.245 --> 05:23.663
<i>"Close at hand"…</i>

05:25.164 --> 05:29.664
<i>Perhaps I'll cross paths with some
new girl visiting from out of town.</i>

05:37.593 --> 05:39.678
Just some dog…

06:00.366 --> 06:02.076
Shigechi!

06:03.035 --> 06:04.494
Oyo?

06:04.662 --> 06:07.039
Josuke, Okuyasu!

06:07.081 --> 06:10.793
Hey, perfect timing, Shigechi.

06:10.877 --> 06:14.088
Let me get right to the point,
we need to borrow some lunch money.

06:14.463 --> 06:16.631
We forgot to bring it.

06:16.716 --> 06:19.260
Huh? What are you talking about?

06:19.427 --> 06:22.805
What happened to all
that money from the lottery?

06:23.055 --> 06:25.640
We deposited all that.

06:25.850 --> 06:28.978
You think we're gonna go all
the way to the bank

06:29.061 --> 06:31.271
just for some lunch money?

06:31.355 --> 06:33.523
A thousand yen will be enough
for both of us.

06:33.608 --> 06:34.859
Yeah.

06:34.942 --> 06:36.276
Come on…

06:36.319 --> 06:38.321
As soon as class is
out we'll head straight to the bank.

06:38.487 --> 06:42.824
Hey, I know that logo…
You got a sandwich from St. Gentlemen!

06:42.950 --> 06:45.160
So they weren't sold out?

06:45.202 --> 06:48.413
Well, you're not gettin' any!
It's mine.

06:48.956 --> 06:52.042
Oh, all right.
I'll lend you the thousand yen…

06:52.960 --> 06:54.878
Now we're talkin'!

06:56.213 --> 06:57.339
Thank you!

06:57.757 --> 07:01.010
I'm writing an i.o.u. for this,

07:01.218 --> 07:02.844
no weaseling out of this one.

07:02.929 --> 07:05.598
Me? You're the biggest weasel
there is!

07:05.848 --> 07:09.518
- Let's see… "June 24th."
- We owe you one, Shigechi.

07:09.560 --> 07:12.646
- "Lent 1,000 yen" … Lent?
- Later!

07:12.688 --> 07:15.941
Now how do you write
the character for "lent" again?

07:16.317 --> 07:17.734
Lent…

07:17.151 --> 07:18.569
LENT

07:17.818 --> 07:18.590
Well, this'll work.

07:19.070 --> 07:20.696
Hiragana works just as well.

07:21.030 --> 07:24.950
I don't know the characters
for "Josuke" or "Okuyasu" either.

07:25.576 --> 07:26.660
Huh?

07:26.911 --> 07:29.288
M-My sandwich…

07:29.330 --> 07:31.040
W-Where'd it go?

07:35.670 --> 07:38.547
<i>Ah, there it is.</i>

07:38.589 --> 07:42.342
<i>I don't remember it
being this faraway, but oh well.</i>

07:51.936 --> 07:53.395
<i>Th-That's…</i>

07:53.896 --> 07:57.900
Hey, Josuke, Okuyasu, wait!

07:58.359 --> 08:00.736
I need your thumbprints
on my i.o.u!

08:00.778 --> 08:02.154
Your thumbprints!

08:06.117 --> 08:08.953
<i>What is that little punk
squealing about?</i>

08:09.036 --> 08:11.413
<i>He took my bag by accident…</i>

08:11.872 --> 08:13.999
Ah, could you be any more annoying.

08:14.083 --> 08:15.751
How the hell do we do that?

08:15.960 --> 08:19.088
You know, you cut your thumb
with a knife…

08:19.255 --> 08:21.715
Okay, now you've gone too far.

08:21.757 --> 08:24.426
Just sign it okay, sign it.

08:24.468 --> 08:28.263
Come on, let's get our asses
to St. Gentlemen. They'll sell out.

08:28.305 --> 08:31.725
<i>Dammit. If he sees
what's in that bag…</i>

08:32.184 --> 08:35.103
<i>She's wearing the ring
I bought her.</i>

08:35.813 --> 08:37.231
<i>It has my fingerprints…</i>

08:37.565 --> 08:39.191
<i>The police will open
an investigation…</i>

08:39.233 --> 08:43.111
<i>It's just a matter of time before
they trace the ring back to me.</i>

08:46.991 --> 08:51.491
<i>Yoshikage Kira has left
not a single clue in fifteen years.</i>

08:53.247 --> 08:55.457
<i>And a pathetic brat
isn't changing that!</i>

08:56.083 --> 08:57.584
Josuke, come on.

08:57.752 --> 08:59.295
Okay.

08:59.378 --> 09:01.797
I'll wait outside.

09:02.506 --> 09:03.798
<i>Now, what to do?</i>

09:04.383 --> 09:06.093
<i>Seize by force it is.</i>

09:06.761 --> 09:09.805
<i>On second thought,
better I snatch it without his knowing.</i>

09:14.810 --> 09:16.311
Shigechi!

09:16.437 --> 09:18.856
You lucky son of a gun.

09:18.939 --> 09:23.401
The St. Gentlemen sandwiches
were already sold out! Shit!

09:23.444 --> 09:26.780
Oh, so they're sold out.

09:26.822 --> 09:29.282
I feel really sorry for you guys.

09:29.325 --> 09:33.825
I guess I could sell you mine
for 10,000 yen.

09:36.999 --> 09:39.334
There's not a decent bone
in your body is there?

09:39.460 --> 09:42.504
Well, Hokaben it is, then, Josuke.

09:42.546 --> 09:44.172
Hokaben, huh?

09:44.256 --> 09:46.883
Nothing we could get for
500 yen and a drink

09:46.967 --> 09:48.551
could ever fill us up.

09:48.803 --> 09:51.806
The cafeteria'll give us plenty of food.

09:51.972 --> 09:54.683
'Sides, Koichi said he'd
get lunch at the cafeteria today.

09:54.725 --> 09:58.270
No way! He'll be eating
with Yukako Yamagishi, right?

09:58.312 --> 10:02.274
Why do I have to be the third wheel
to those honeymooners' lovefest?

10:02.483 --> 10:04.443
What's worse, the school serves

10:04.485 --> 10:07.654
one-millimeter-thick meat,

10:07.696 --> 10:10.615
and who knows what
the hell they put in that miso soup?

10:10.741 --> 10:13.577
Hey, the equipment room at
my middle school's gym

10:13.661 --> 10:15.829
has a ton of drinks.

10:16.038 --> 10:20.333
Our P.E. teacher always sneaks away
to have coffee and tea in there.

10:20.751 --> 10:24.296
All of the teachers are in
the faculty room during lunch,

10:24.505 --> 10:28.217
so I sneak in through the window
sometimes and take some.

10:28.300 --> 10:31.261
Why don't you guys go buy a lunch
and we'll go there together.

10:31.345 --> 10:35.223
You're stealing from school?

10:35.307 --> 10:37.183
You are a stingy bastard.

10:37.184 --> 10:39.019
You can't even buy your own drinks?

10:39.061 --> 10:41.605
You'll never see me
do something that greedy.

10:41.689 --> 10:42.731
See ya!

10:43.190 --> 10:46.568
I was just trying to be nice…

10:47.319 --> 10:51.239
Okay. You better pay me back
my thousand yen tomorrow!

11:03.377 --> 11:05.253
Oh, I'm very sorry, sir!

11:05.421 --> 11:08.215
I wasn't looking where I was going.

11:08.382 --> 11:09.758
Really sorry.

11:10.885 --> 11:14.179
<i>Shit, shit…
He's left his idiotic friends,</i>

11:14.221 --> 11:15.764
<i>but he's heading back to school.</i>

11:16.348 --> 11:18.683
<i>He's going to eat lunch at school…</i>

11:18.934 --> 11:20.143
<i>What to do?</i>

11:21.145 --> 11:25.645
BUDOGAOKA MIDDLE SCHOOL

11:21.312 --> 11:23.939
<i>So they call him "Shigechi"…</i>

11:24.023 --> 11:25.482
<i>There's no question…</i>

11:25.566 --> 11:28.193
<i>In a matter of minutes,
he will open that bag…</i>

11:28.944 --> 11:31.176
<i>This is unfathomable.</i>

11:47.338 --> 11:51.838
Yes, yes… No one's gonna
bother me and my lunch in here.

12:00.768 --> 12:03.312
Oh yeah, that's right!

12:03.354 --> 12:06.648
Before I eat,
I need to make my coffee.

12:06.815 --> 12:10.735
I didn't come all the way here
for nothing.

12:16.367 --> 12:18.827
How very fortunate, Shigechi.

12:19.286 --> 12:23.331
Had you peaked inside,
I would've had to obliterate you.

12:29.546 --> 12:31.673
Hey, Josuke! We're here!

12:33.968 --> 12:36.136
- It's smaller than I thought…
<i>- W-What?</i>

12:36.303 --> 12:39.472
<i>They're not supposed to be here!</i>

12:42.017 --> 12:44.352
Shigechi, you here?

12:44.436 --> 12:45.728
Shigechi!

12:45.938 --> 12:50.275
Oh, what're you and Josuke
doing here?

12:50.317 --> 12:54.195
We decided we couldn't
pass up some coffee from cafe gym.

12:54.321 --> 12:57.449
We got 500-yen Makunouchi bentos!

12:58.409 --> 13:02.909
Hmph. This after
you called me a greedy thief…

13:03.831 --> 13:05.874
Self-righteous pricks!

13:05.916 --> 13:08.418
Come on, give us a break.

13:08.669 --> 13:12.172
Haven't you heard of people
changing their minds?

13:14.717 --> 13:16.009
<i>What to do?</i>

13:16.135 --> 13:20.635
<i>Offing one of them
would be a picnic, but not three.</i>

13:20.889 --> 13:25.268
<i>Shit!
And she's only centimeters away…</i>

13:29.023 --> 13:32.067
Shigechi, don't forget
my drink, too.

13:32.276 --> 13:34.361
No coffee for me.
Make it green tea.

13:34.486 --> 13:36.571
Got any black tea?
I want some milk in it.

13:36.613 --> 13:40.992
Blech. Makunouchi with milk tea?
That's gross.

13:41.201 --> 13:45.121
<i>Shit! He's gonna eat right
on top of this thing.</i>

13:45.247 --> 13:49.417
<i>At this rate, he's going to
open the bag in front of all of them!</i>

13:58.218 --> 14:00.720
Aw, soy sauce again.

14:01.013 --> 14:03.598
They always put soy sauce
with katsu.

14:03.682 --> 14:05.934
Huh? You always eat katsu
with soy sauce.

14:06.101 --> 14:07.811
What?! You jackass!

14:07.895 --> 14:09.688
Everyone knows
it's tonkatsu sauce!

14:09.730 --> 14:13.024
Putting soy sauce on
tonkatsu violates all that is sacred.

14:13.233 --> 14:14.525
Who cares?

14:21.325 --> 14:22.534
<i>Yes!</i>

14:28.624 --> 14:29.708
<i>W-What?</i>

14:34.421 --> 14:35.713
<i>Dammit!</i>

14:36.131 --> 14:37.048
What?

14:43.055 --> 14:47.059
MORIOH LANDMARK #7
"BAKERY ST. GENTLEMEN"
HOW TO GET THERE: TAKE THE "MORIOH
BUDOGAOKA HIGH SCHOOL" BUS
TO ITS FINAL STOP AND
WALK TWO MINUTES ON
THE GREEN ROAD FROM THE STATION.
STUDENTS, HOUSEWIVES,
AND OFFICE LADIES RAVE ABOUT
ITS VARIETY OF STONE-OVEN BAKED BREADS.
DON'T MISS THEIR BEST SELLER:
SANDWICHES. BEWARE, THEY SELL OUT FAST.

14:49.353 --> 14:50.437
<i>Dammit!</i>

14:50.813 --> 14:51.814
What?

15:01.490 --> 15:04.993
Hey! Just what do you
think you're doing, Josuke?

15:05.119 --> 15:09.619
Hey! It looks a lot like
someone trying to steal a sandwich to me.

15:10.040 --> 15:12.834
No! Quit being so stupid.

15:12.835 --> 15:15.337
I thought I heard something weird,

15:15.421 --> 15:17.256
I was just gonna take
a quick look.

15:17.297 --> 15:19.048
It's totally off limits!

15:19.133 --> 15:21.593
I know you wouldn't just
look at it!

15:21.760 --> 15:24.888
Teriyaki chicken sandwiches
are my favorite,

15:24.930 --> 15:29.017
give me a teeny-weeny
bite, is exactly what you'll say.

15:29.768 --> 15:31.936
You sure are
a greedy little stinker, aren't you?

15:32.146 --> 15:33.730
Where the hell's my tea? Remember?

15:34.148 --> 15:35.691
Milk tea for me.

15:35.691 --> 15:37.526
I'm making them.

15:42.865 --> 15:43.615
<i>Now!</i>

15:51.832 --> 15:53.291
<i>I did it.</i>

15:53.542 --> 15:55.126
Get 'em while they're hot.

15:55.169 --> 15:57.546
One green tea and one milk tea.

15:57.671 --> 15:58.505
Ooooh…

15:58.547 --> 15:59.548
Thank you!

16:02.009 --> 16:02.968
What's with you?

16:03.093 --> 16:07.055
M-My sandwich?
What'd you do with it?

16:07.264 --> 16:09.057
Huh? Oh…

16:09.141 --> 16:10.767
So it is gone.

16:10.893 --> 16:13.770
But we don't know what
happened to it, right, Okuyasu?

16:14.146 --> 16:14.896
Yeah.

16:14.980 --> 16:16.481
All right, enough of the games!

16:16.648 --> 16:20.068
You have to know.
You're the only ones here!

16:20.110 --> 16:22.362
No, seriously, we don't!

16:22.404 --> 16:24.906
Really, we're not messing around.

16:25.032 --> 16:27.409
No joke, we really
don't know what's going on.

16:27.493 --> 16:31.747
Y-You ass wipes…
I-I'm gonna get really mad!

16:31.914 --> 16:33.290
It's the truth!

16:33.373 --> 16:35.708
All right, I've had about enough.

16:35.834 --> 16:37.669
Why would we take your sandwich—

16:37.711 --> 16:41.131
Lie all you want,
I'll find out soon enough!

16:41.215 --> 16:44.509
All I have to do is have
Harvest turn this room inside out!

16:44.551 --> 16:47.595
Damn you're annoying!
Fine, do it!

16:47.679 --> 16:50.973
I want you to!
Look all you want.

16:51.183 --> 16:53.935
You think we'd steal
that stupid thing?

17:00.567 --> 17:05.067
<i>What? I can't see what
they're doing from in here.</i>

17:06.740 --> 17:10.785
<i>What is that little pissant up to?</i>

17:10.911 --> 17:11.995
Hey!

17:12.079 --> 17:14.706
I know somebody's in here!

17:15.207 --> 17:16.958
It's the P.E. teacher!

17:17.042 --> 17:19.461
It's time to bail, Shigechi!

17:19.545 --> 17:22.172
B-But my sandwich!

17:22.256 --> 17:24.299
Now's not the time!

17:25.259 --> 17:26.843
You wait!

17:30.222 --> 17:32.474
Damn, snot-nosed kids.

17:32.641 --> 17:35.518
I thought my tea and
coffee wasn't lasting very long.

17:35.602 --> 17:38.855
I thought I was going crazy.
No wonder.

17:40.566 --> 17:43.485
I gotta start locking
this sucker up like Fort Knox.

17:56.164 --> 17:57.832
<i>Much ado about nothing…</i>

17:58.125 --> 18:02.625
<i>I beat the odds,
and got back my girl.</i>

18:03.547 --> 18:05.715
<i>I've always had this feeling…</i>

18:05.966 --> 18:10.466
<i>That looking over Yoshikage Kira's
shoulder is a guardian angel…</i>

18:11.805 --> 18:16.305
<i>That living each and every
day with rigor and boldness,</i>

18:17.185 --> 18:20.771
<i>will deliver me from
a life of unhappiness.</i>

18:23.150 --> 18:24.693
<i>That was close.</i>

18:25.027 --> 18:28.196
<i>I knew you'd come back to me.</i>

18:31.158 --> 18:32.868
Found it!

18:34.494 --> 18:38.873
Now why is there
a stranger holding my sandwich?

18:38.915 --> 18:43.415
And why is there some strange man
hanging around my middle school?

18:45.672 --> 18:50.172
You wouldn't happen to
be talking to me, would you, little boy?

18:50.469 --> 18:53.013
Because I have not the slightest idea
what you're going on about.

18:53.138 --> 18:54.931
This is my sandwich.

18:55.182 --> 18:57.350
I just purchased the item
at St. Gentlemen.

18:57.517 --> 19:00.520
Wrong, that bag belongs to me!

19:00.562 --> 19:03.231
And I have my reasons
for saying so!

19:03.315 --> 19:05.942
Not that you'd ever understand.

19:06.193 --> 19:09.237
It's time to take back
what's ours, Harvest!

19:10.989 --> 19:15.489
W-What? What's happening?
They're pulling my bag…

19:22.542 --> 19:26.837
W-Wha—?! W-What…
My sandwich…

19:27.339 --> 19:31.839
Is this… a real hand from
a real person?

19:34.221 --> 19:37.432
Low and behold.
You've seen what you cannot unsee.

19:37.766 --> 19:42.266
And it seems, little boy,
that you and I share a unique power.

19:44.064 --> 19:47.025
You can see my Harvest?

19:47.067 --> 19:49.944
H-Hey, what's this hand?

19:50.028 --> 19:53.740
Why are you walking around
with a hand in your bag?

19:53.865 --> 19:57.410
You are by yourself now,
I presume? Your two friends…

19:57.536 --> 20:00.121
I believe you referred
to them as Josuke and Okuyasu?

20:00.330 --> 20:03.416
Shall I assume they have
a similar power?

20:04.084 --> 20:06.586
Hey! You stay right there!

20:07.421 --> 20:10.132
If you so much as blink,
you're a goner!

20:10.257 --> 20:12.842
You're a super weirdo!

20:12.926 --> 20:16.387
And I don't want you
coming any closer!

20:16.555 --> 20:19.641
You're really starting to
make my skin crawl!

20:19.766 --> 20:23.436
Don't move!
I said stay right there!

20:25.480 --> 20:29.817
I'm Yoshikage Kira, age 33.

20:30.068 --> 20:33.654
I live in northeast
Morioh's villa district,

20:33.822 --> 20:35.532
and I am not married.

20:38.118 --> 20:41.162
I work for Kameyu department stores,

20:41.288 --> 20:44.749
and I return home
no later than 8 PM.

20:46.752 --> 20:50.088
I don't smoke,
but enjoy the occasional libation.

20:50.380 --> 20:52.632
I'm in bed by 11 PM,

20:52.674 --> 20:56.302
and am sure to sleep
a solid eight hours.

20:57.471 --> 20:59.848
If I indulge in
a warm glass of milk

21:00.015 --> 21:04.102
then stretch for
about twenty minutes,

21:04.227 --> 21:06.479
sweet, sweet dreams
are usually the result.

21:07.898 --> 21:12.398
I awake like a newborn
baby, refreshed and recharged.

21:13.528 --> 21:16.531
I was given a clean
bill of health at my last checkup.

21:16.615 --> 21:20.160
W-What is all this about?!

21:20.452 --> 21:24.952
I have lived my life in pursuit
of inner peace.

21:27.000 --> 21:31.087
I choose not to concern myself
with winning or losing,

21:31.171 --> 21:34.299
life's troubles, or enemies
who bring sleepless nights.

21:34.549 --> 21:38.511
That is my social-coping mechanism,

21:38.887 --> 21:42.807
and that is what brings me happiness.

21:44.184 --> 21:48.684
Of course, if I were ever to
engage in combat, I would never lose.

21:56.780 --> 21:58.740
In other words, Shigechi,

21:58.865 --> 22:02.368
you are a troublemaker
who could hinder my sleep.

22:02.410 --> 22:04.286
You are the enemy.

22:07.624 --> 22:09.417
Th-That's…

22:09.459 --> 22:13.959
Deadly Queen…
I named him myself.

22:15.549 --> 22:18.468
Before you utter a word of this
to another soul,

22:18.552 --> 22:21.221
I will eradicate you.

22:21.304 --> 22:24.807
I will sleep soundly tonight.

23:38.298 --> 23:41.509
EPISODE 22
YOSHIKAGE KIRA JUST
WANTS TO LIVE QUIETLY, PART 2
